{"run_analyses":["H130","H131","H132","H133","H134","H135","H136","H137","H138","H139"],"narrative":"No assessments are due. I request the ten active, previously untested claims registered in this iteration. The analyses partition natural-log progression-free survival at its observed median and test whether the replicated but subthreshold feature_003 contrast is clinically localized to the shorter-PFS half. H130 and H131 estimate the feature_003 mean difference in the lower and higher log-PFS strata, respectively; H132 tests whether the lower-PFS contrast exceeds its higher-PFS complement in the claimed negative raw direction. This is a more informative follow-up than another broad screen because feature_003 is currently the main unresolved candidate and the PFS partition has direct clinical interpretation.

I also test whether the three large core associations are stable across the clinically shorter-PFS stratum and whether their raw effects are meaningfully modified by log-PFS. H136-H138 estimate feature_010, feature_002, and feature_037 effects in the lower-PFS half. Their accepted marginal effects are far above threshold, so the scientific purpose is to verify persistence rather than re-test a marginal claim. H133-H135 directly assess interaction magnitude, using higher-PFS complement for the positive feature_010 and feature_002 claims and lower-PFS subgroup for the negative raw feature_037 claim. A large signed interaction would establish a dataset-specific effect modification; near-zero interactions would further support additive observational structure. These analyses use the same supplied data and remain association-only, not causal or mechanistic claims.

Finally, H139 directly compares feature_046 level_003 with level_002. This is the most useful clarification of the unresolved level_003-versus-level_001 near-threshold signal because it can distinguish a distinct level_003 contrast from a diffuse subthreshold categorical pattern. The nominal labels are not treated as ordered, and acceptance will require the direct level_003-minus-level_002 lower bound to exceed +0.15 composite dependency-score units in the claimed direction. I do not rerun already evidenced or validated claims because that adds no new sample, and I do not allocate the current batch to closed low-priority untested screens: the available evidence already shows those effects, when observed, are small and far below threshold, whereas the ten selected comparisons address the remaining unresolved feature_003 candidate, core-effect stability, and the feature_046 ambiguity.","research_notes":"Running H130-H139: feature_003 localization by median feature_040 log-PFS; core-predictor persistence and interaction by feature_040; feature_046 level_003 vs level_002. Existing accepted robust associations: feature_010=1 and feature_002=1 higher outcome_001, feature_037=1 lower raw outcome_001/stronger dependency. Feature_003 remains near-threshold and unresolved. Decision rule after appraise: accept/validation candidate only if lower CI exceeds +0.15 in claimed direction and estimate is not selected solely by weak upper tail. If feature_003 lower-PFS mean is threshold-level and H132 interaction supports it, request targeted validation of that specific stratum; if only point estimate exceeds threshold but lower bound is below +0.15, keep unresolved/closed. Feature_046 H139 can clarify H68/H67; accept only if direct level_003 vs level_002 lower bound exceeds +0.15. Do not rerun tested core strata or old low-prevalence screens without a new scientific rationale."}
